.SH NAME
md_CODE__OF__CONDUCT \- 📜 SystemEx Code of Conduct 
.PP

.SH "Overview"
.PP
The \fBSystemEx\fP project is committed to providing a respectful, safe, and constructive environment for everyone interacting with the repository, including issue reports, discussions, pull requests, and general communication\&.

.PP
\fBSystemEx\fP is a personal hobby project developed by a single intersex author; my pronouns are dey/deren/dem/dem\&. While I aim for correctness, determinism, and clean architecture, not every issue may be visible immediately, and responses or fixes may occasionally be delayed\&. Constructive feedback, improvement ideas, and technical discussions are always welcome\&.
.SH "1\&. Expected Behavior"
.PP
All participants are expected to:

.PP
.IP "\(bu" 2
Treat others with respect and professionalism 
.br

.IP "\(bu" 2
Engage in constructive, technical discussion 
.br

.IP "\(bu" 2
Assume good intent and communicate clearly 
.br

.IP "\(bu" 2
Provide actionable, specific feedback 
.br

.IP "\(bu" 2
Respect architectural decisions and design choices 
.br

.IP "\(bu" 2
Keep interactions focused on the project and its goals 
.br

.PP
.SH "2\&. Unacceptable Behavior"
.PP
The following behaviors are not tolerated:

.PP
.IP "\(bu" 2
Harassment, insults, or personal attacks 
.br

.IP "\(bu" 2
Discriminatory language or behavior 
.br

.IP "\(bu" 2
Dismissing or belittling contributors 
.br

.IP "\(bu" 2
Aggressive or hostile communication 
.br

.IP "\(bu" 2
Spamming issues, discussions, or pull requests 
.br

.IP "\(bu" 2
Intentionally breaking builds or sabotaging code 
.br

.IP "\(bu" 2
Large unsolicited refactors that ignore project structure 
.br

.PP
.SH "3\&. Technical Collaboration Guidelines"
.PP
.SS "3\&.1 Be precise"
When reporting issues or proposing changes, please include:

.PP
.IP "\(bu" 2
A clear description 
.br

.IP "\(bu" 2
Reproduction steps (if applicable) 
.br

.IP "\(bu" 2
Expected vs\&. actual behavior 
.br

.IP "\(bu" 2
Relevant code snippets or logs 
.br

.PP
.SS "3\&.2 Respect modular design"
\fBSystemEx\fP intentionally avoids deep cross‑dependencies\&. 
.br
 Some components exist in multiple forms (e\&.g\&., \fRMap<TKey, TValue>\fP based on \fRPair<TKey, TValue>[]\fP instead of \fRVector<Pair<\&.\&.\&.>>\fP) to keep subsystems isolated and easier to debug\&. 
.br
 This is a deliberate architectural choice\&.
.SS "3\&.3 Discuss major changes first"
Large refactors or structural changes should be discussed before implementation to avoid regressions\&.
.SH "4\&. Reporting Issues"
.PP
If you observe unacceptable behavior or have concerns:

.PP
.IP "\(bu" 2
Open an issue in the repository 
.br

.IP "\(bu" 2
Provide context and details 
.br

.IP "\(bu" 2
Remain respectful and factual 
.br

.PP

.PP
Reports will be reviewed as time permits\&.
.SH "5\&. Enforcement"
.PP
Violations of this Code of Conduct may result in:

.PP
.IP "\(bu" 2
A request to modify behavior 
.br

.IP "\(bu" 2
Temporary communication restrictions 
.br

.IP "\(bu" 2
Removal of comments or contributions 
.br

.IP "\(bu" 2
Blocking from the repository in severe cases 
.br

.PP

.PP
Enforcement decisions are made at the discretion of the project maintainer\&.
.SH "6\&. Acknowledgment"
.PP
Thank you for contributing to a respectful, collaborative, and technically focused environment\&. 
.br
 Your participation helps \fBSystemEx\fP grow as a stable, deterministic, and modular low‑level framework for \&.NET\&. 
